  "purpose": "Measure definitions lost per malformed file, rather than whether other files still parse. Six hand-written fixtures each carry exactly one fault and state their prediction in their own header. Single-character faults are then injected into real corpus files at their first, middle, and last definition, and the surviving definition count is compared against a clean parse of the same file. The truncation-at-last case is the positive control: recovery can reach nothing after it, so the lexer must lose exactly the definition that was cut and the tape must lose the file.",
